509 0 obj
<< /BS << /W 0 >> /F 4 /FT /Btn /Ff 65536 /MK << /BC [ 0 0 0 0 ] >> /P 206 0 R /Rect [ 85.199997 492.16495 510.47998 584.804965 ] /Subtype /Widget /T (Figure1) /TU (Flowchart depicting a process where a prompt with multiple-choice question options \(A, B, C, D\) is input into an LLM \(large language model\), which then produces a generated answer. Arrows indicate the flow from the prompt to the LLM and finally to the answer.) /Type /Annot >>
endobj
510 0 obj
<< /BS << /W 0 >> /F 4 /FT /Btn /Ff 65536 /MK << /BC [ 0 0 0 0 ] >> /P 206 0 R /Rect [ 56.696999 248.984958 538.617004 418.42496 ] /Subtype /Widget /T (Figure2) /TU (Flowchart illustrating the process of solving a multiple-choice question using SymPy and LLM. It starts with a prompt asking if the question can be solved with SymPy. If yes, a Python script is written to solve it, using the Python interpreter. The calculated answer is matched to answer options by an LLM, leading to a generated answer. If no, the LLM chooses the single best answer based on question and options.) /Type /Annot >>
endobj
